Sensor Catalog & Entity Specification
  
1. Catalog Configuration (YAML)
The system initializes devices based on a central catalog. For simulation purposes, base_val and noise are utilized to generate synthetic telemetry using Gaussian distribution.

Schema Requirements

Key,Type,Description
key,string,Unique identifier for the device instance.
name,string,Human-readable display name.
device_class,string,Functional category (must match SensorDeviceClass).
unit,string,"Physical unit of measurement (e.g., °C, %)."
base_val,float,Baseline value for simulation.
noise,float,Standard deviation for Gaussian noise generation.
  
Configuration Example

YAML
sensors:
  - key: "temp_01"
    name: "Temperature"
    device_class: "temperature"
    unit: "°C"
    base_val: 26.0
    noise: 0.3
      
2. Implementation Logic
Device Class Enumeration

Strictly defines the supported physical categories to ensure data consistency.

Sensors:

class SensorDeviceClass(StrEnum):
    TEMPERATURE = "temperature"
    HUMIDITY = "humidity"
    AQI = "aqi"
    PM25 = "pm25"

Actuators:

class ActuatorDeviceClass(StrEnum):
    SWITCH = "switch"   # Fans
    CLIMATE = "climate" # AC units

      
Metadata Container

A decoupled dataclass that separates static configuration from operational runtime logic.
      
Sensors:

@dataclass
class SensorEntityDescription:
    key: str
    device_class: SensorDeviceClass | None = None
    native_unit_of_measurement: str | None = None
    name: str | None = None

Actuators:

@dataclass
class ActuatorEntityDescription:
    key: str
    name: str
    device_class: ActuatorDeviceClass
